A||N||22||AusFiero||Loki's Wish - Wilder stage 2 body mods. Which bits do people like?||||5||
Z||000000||AusFiero||05-13-2001||11:51 AM||||Or dislike for that matter.<P>I suppose this is the only way to find out what people want. Throw the ideas around. What is the prefered features out of this lot of ideas for a front look?<P>Yes Loki you got your way  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>These mods would involve more cutting of the original nose cone. The indicator lenses have been changed to clear with orange bulbs. Or install driving lights. Get a glass shop to drill 2 holes in the driving lights. Install 2 more globe holders with orange globes and your driving lights double as indicators. The holes in the lower spolier sections could be ducted for brake cooling or used as a very good position to install small spotlight style fog lights. <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stage2-101.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stage2-102.jpg"> <BR>The top nose vents in this shot would be functional cooling vents.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stage2-103.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stage2-104.jpg"> <BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero.gif"> <BR>When I was young I spent 80% of my money on Women, Gambling and Alcohol. I guess I wasted the rest.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Bluebottlejunky||05-13-2001||12:11 PM||||I love it man!  Id like the last one with the mess grill and those hood scoops!  very sweet..but I bet if you made them they would cost a ton!<P>------------------<BR>Mike<BR>85'GT 4sp, <BR>AOL IM: Fierofanatic2001||||reg||1
Z||000002||Spektyr||05-13-2001||01:29 PM||||All of them are great options, I'll just say that I don't like the 'cross' style intake, it looks too much like a Dodge. (IMHO)<P>Also, my understanding of the front airflow is that the problem lies in evacuating air from the backside of the radiator.  Now if you reversed the hood vents it not only solves that problem, but helps evacuate air from under the front of the car (and according to many people improving handling at speed).  I know my car gets pretty scary at speed as air builds up under the front and makes the front end feel lighter.||||reg||1
